│ Foundation. RESULTS At school, half-day children consumed up to 25% of the daily recommendation for energy and       │
│ nutrients, while all-day children achieved at least a third of the recommended intakes. When intakes at home and     │
│ school were combined, all three groups of children (AM, PM and all-day) exceeded dietary recommendations for         │
│ protein, vitamins and minerals. Energy intake remained below 100% of the recommendation, while intake of total fat,  │
