care feasible, family-based behavioral intervention, targeting both young children and their parent, in promoting       
healthy weight change. Participants are 270 overweight and obese children (ages 4 to 7 years) and their parents, who    
were recruited from a primarily African American urban population. Parents and children were instructed in proven       
cognitive behavioral techniques (e.g. goal setting, self-talk, stimulus control and reinforcement) designed to encourage
healthier food choices (more whole grains, fruits and vegetables, and less concentrated fats and sugar), reduce portion 
